#{[17592186341734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186341059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341734 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341734 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341734 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186340465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341734 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c9c05c61-b32b-5fe2-821b-e8f8f940b2d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186341051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186340635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341793 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e86449e4-c0a9-5b52-a8c2-80a206761f0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341844 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341844 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72684" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341844 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341844 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=4$ for all partition $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341844 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3273cb89-af5d-5582-86a1-9111196782fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341844 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =4({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =4(4-0)(6-2) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=64\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 64=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=64.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341884 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341884 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72906" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341884 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341884 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-5,-1]\\times [0,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341884 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6a79a2d-bcfd-5ef3-be20-8c72ffbf021f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341884 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le 5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le \\frac{5}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{5}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le \\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{5}{2}((-1)^{2}-(-5)^{2})(3-0)=-180 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})(-1-(-5))=36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le -180+36\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le -144\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-144.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186366266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366261 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e7b4be15-0b1e-5f67-9b68-ce3d1e514c8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366262 #edb/ref 1080 "60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366262 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366262 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3353ca9f-51ab-51a8-9174-44f6fb3eee84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366263 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366263 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366263 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b35cb88b-3972-5e20-9788-60b4ea9b4c15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366264 #edb/ref 1080 "15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366264 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366264 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6d1b0a7a-b80d-5f8b-976e-7e14027e1304" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366265 #edb/ref 1080 "30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366265 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366265 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6e3cef94-383f-5d00-8fa0-399009bcce6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366266 #edb/ref 1080 "45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366266 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366266 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f3d468b6-4275-521c-b7f4-abeadf8f00f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371679 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371679 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123853" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371679 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371679 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[5,6]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371679 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eeafd037-077a-51ed-84eb-4b9e62434000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371679 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n2{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}\\le 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n2{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}\\le ({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{3}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{3}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}-\\frac{3}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({6}^{2}-{5}^{2})(3-1)=22 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{3}{2}({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})(6-5)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 22-12\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 10\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=10.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186371682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371680 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7d7848e2-f768-55a9-aff3-ed72e02a83b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371681 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371681 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186